  "fieldOverrides": [
    {
      "//": "A SECOND DEVICE does not know its own local id yet, so it cannot address its identity document at users/{localId}/profile/self - it has to find it by COLLECTION GROUP. A single-field index is automatic for a collection but NOT for a collection group, and it is configured HERE rather than under \"indexes\": Firestore rejects a one-field entry there with 'this index is not necessary, configure using single field index controls'. The array-contains clause in the query is not optional either - rules REJECT a query they cannot prove rather than filtering it, and the read rule tests visibleTo. See services/firebase/firebaseProfile.ts.",
      "collectionGroup": "profile",
      "fieldPath": "visibleTo",
      "indexes": [
        {
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS",
          "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "//": "PULL INDEXES ARE GENERATED FROM syncPaths.SYNC_PATHS, one per live leaf collection. A pull query is where(visibleTo array-contains uid) + orderBy(syncedAt) + orderBy(__name__), and that combination needs a COMPOSITE index at COLLECTION_GROUP scope - a single-field index is automatic for a collection but never for a collection group, and __name__ is supplied implicitly as the last field of a composite. A regression check fails if a table is in the map with no entry here and no read block in firestore.rules."
}
